 "exemplars": {
  "0": [
   {
    "context": "Let's go to Ephesians 2, 8 through 9. For by grace you have been saved through faith, and this is not your own doing. It is the gift of God, not because of works, lest any man should boast. Many Protestants think this verse refutes Catholic views on salvation because they only think about our initial salvation, the moment we go from being a child of wrath to being a child of God.",
    "dist": 0.3483,
    "occurrence_id": 84089,
    "published_at": "2025-12-02T18:45:03Z",
    "role": "host",
    "surface": "grace",
    "t": 2.16,
    "title": "Does Catholicism teach works save you?",
    "video_id": "c2X21fTLfx8"
   },
   {
    "context": "Otherwise, as the same apostle says, grace is no more grace, quoting Romans 11:6. As I noted in my previous episode about Ephesians 2, 8 through 9, the church teaches that we are initially justified by grace alone, apart from faith or works. We simply receive God's gift of saving grace in baptism. There is no work like circumcision, or even a good deed like feeding the poor, that we must do in order to go from being dead in sin to being alive in Christ. The catechism of the Catholic Church says the following Moved by grace, man turns toward God and away from sin, thus accepting forgiveness and righteousness from on high.",
    "dist": 0.3518,
    "occurrence_id": 2763,
    "published_at": "2025-04-30T13:00:05Z",
    "role": "host",
    "surface": "grace",
    "t": 1147.68,
    "title": "Protestants Still Can't Explain James 2",
    "video_id": "0LwEgFig00A"
   },
   {
    "context": "Third, the catechism says, no one can merit the initial grace of forgiveness and justification at the beginning of conversion. So we are not saved by grace plus merit. But as I showed in my video on Mike Winger recently, we can merit eternal life by cooperating with God's grace and following God's commands to keep his commandments. And in doing so, God keeps his promise towards us and gives us eternal life for following his commands.",
    "dist": 0.3769,
    "occurrence_id": 44825,
    "published_at": "2022-03-14T13:00:09Z",
    "role": "host",
    "surface": "grace",
    "t": 1319.44,
    "title": "REBUTTING “American Gospel” on Catholic salvation",
    "video_id": "JddkPla-pis"
   },
   {
    "context": "Right? Yeah. I mean, Paul says if if uh righteousness or if uh righteousness could be acquired through the law, then Christ died in vain. Ladies and gentlemen, you realize that grace is what's unique about Christianity. I mean, it's true, that's another thing unique, but Christianity is the only worldview where you don't work your way to God, God works his way to you, he pays the price for your sin.",
    "dist": 0.3802,
    "occurrence_id": 29247,
    "published_at": "2025-04-26T01:00:06Z",
    "role": "unknown",
    "surface": "grace",
    "t": 2766.4,
    "title": "[PODCAST] Cults and Worldviews: Why Do They Matter? with Dr. Brady Blevins @WatchmanFellowshipInc",
    "video_id": "CuVr8-zw84A"
   },
   {
    "context": "And all he wants to emphasize is that given our fallenness and sinfulness, um our experiential knowledge of God will not be complete through natural theology. We need God's grace to work in our heart. And in my theology, I would say that God's will is that all persons be saved and come to a knowledge of the truth, and that therefore he bestows on all persons sufficient grace to come to saving faith if they will respond to God's gracious initiatives.",
    "dist": 0.382,
    "occurrence_id": 117806,
    "published_at": "2024-03-05T20:00:21Z",
    "role": "host",
    "surface": "grace",
    "t": 927.76,
    "title": "Natural Theology and Luther | Reasonable Faith Podcast",
    "video_id": "s625IbNvQLQ"
   }
  ],
  "1": [
   {
    "context": "And I said, listen, we've got to come to terms with understanding who we are. Either we're saved or we're not saved. We're we're we're holy or we're not holy. We're this or that. And what I was trying to say was, hey, as far as grace is concerned, if you're saved, then nothing else matters. If you mess up, you mess up. Just come to terms with the fact that you're either saved or you're not. If you are great, just let everything else go. You don't gotta do, you don't got to jump through hoops. You don't gotta do all this praying, you don't got to do all this fasting, you don't got to do all this Bible study, you don't gotta come to church.",
    "dist": 0.4375,
    "occurrence_id": 55812,
    "published_at": "2025-06-15T19:11:29Z",
    "role": "unknown",
    "surface": "grace",
    "t": 3178.48,
    "title": "Building \"No King\" Communities with X-Pastor Kyle Butler // Sunday Sessions",
    "video_id": "OriYFVxm7gE"
   },
   {
    "context": "I don't want to ever let my heart get callous to what Jesus did for me. No one is ever beyond the reach. It also shows me we can't quantify God's grace. It doesn't make sense how great God's grace is. That's how you know it's grace. It's too good to be true. We're bringing this shroud everywhere. So just follow me on social um and just pray for me because um, you know, there's a lot of attack as well. So um I want to continue to be as bold as I can for the resurrection of Christ. Give us your website so people can learn more and find out where the tour is going.",
    "dist": 0.4414,
    "occurrence_id": 116200,
    "published_at": "2026-04-07T22:30:06Z",
    "role": "host",
